Main method `saveOwner(Owner owner, boolean sharesHousehold)` — lines 280-318 (`@Transactional`):

```java
@Override
@Transactional
public void saveOwner(Owner owner, boolean sharesHousehold) throws DataAccessException {
    boolean isCreate = owner.isNew();
    assertEmailDomainAllowed(owner);
    assertIdentityIsUnique(owner);
    if (owner.isNew()) {
        assertCityHasCapacity(owner);
        if (!sharesHousehold) {
            assertHouseholdIsUnique(owner);
        }
    }
    if (owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {
        owner.setRegistrationDate(LocalDate.now());
    }
    assertRegistrationDateNotInFuture(owner);
    owner.setRegistrationDate(rollToBusinessDay(owner.getRegistrationDate()));
    if (owner.isNew()) {
        assertDailyRegistrationLimit(owner);
        owner.setBulkSignupWarning(computeBulkSignupWarning(owner));
    }
    if (owner.isNew() && owner.getCustomerCode() == null) {
        owner.setCustomerCode(generateCustomerCode(owner));
    }
    if (owner.isNew() && owner.getNamesakeCount() == null) {
        owner.setNamesakeCount(countNamesakes(owner));
    }
    if (owner.isNew() && owner.getHouseholdCount() == null) {
        owner.setHouseholdCount(countHouseholdMembers(owner));
    }
    if (owner.isNew()) {
        assignPossibleDuplicate(owner, sharesHousehold);
    }
    ownerRepository.save(owner);
    if (isCreate) {
        AUDIT.info("owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}",
            owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());
    }
}
```

Validation / business-rule checks invoked, in order (all in the same file):

1. `assertEmailDomainAllowed(owner)` — lines 416-420. Throws `DisposableEmailDomainException` if `Owner.isDisposableEmailDomain(email)` (blocklist: mailinator.com, tempmail.com, guerrillamail.com).
2. `assertIdentityIsUnique(owner)` — lines 436-449. Normalizes telephone; if another owner has the same normalized telephone, throws `DuplicateIdentityException`.
3. `assertCityHasCapacity(owner)` (create only) — lines 480-492. Throws `CityAtCapacityException` when the city already has ≥ `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY` (50) owners.
4. `assertHouseholdIsUnique(owner)` (create only, unless `sharesHousehold`) — lines 460-473. Throws `DuplicateIdentityException` if another owner shares the household id (same lastName + postcode).
5. Default `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` if null — lines 292-294.
